<title>USA: Tower Semiconductor says names new cfo.</title>
<headline>Tower Semiconductor says names new cfo.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tower Semiconductor said Tuesday that it named Gil Pinto as its chief financial officer.</p>
<p>The Israeli based computer chip maker, originally issued a press release in Migdal Haemark, Israel.  The company was not available to say whom Pinto replaced or where he was last employed.</p>
<p>The company also reported a 62 percent increase in net income for the second quarter.  Net income rose to $0.37 per share, or $4.90 million from $0.23 or $3.0 million during the same period a year ago.</p>
</text>
